#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114870 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "5e2f19a2-f9e3-59dd-83a9-90950b0a55a8" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-20883" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=-2(7^x)-1$." :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=2(7^x)$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/c0bddb97a59f1d1446397be26bf1e51e.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-2(7^x)$. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,2)$ to $(0,-2)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/f447f1ce83ec1094829ff62c4504ced3.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit down to give $y=-2(7^x)-1$. The point $(0,-2)$ moves to $(0,-3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/6743dca8e28aed3836687c609186c041.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114871 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f4440-ba1a-58ce-9ff2-ccdf591a0d30" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Decay Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "0ab5addd-b4b1-56b8-8cd2-690d5be81b8a" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-20884" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y = -\\left(\\dfrac 12 \\right)^x + 2$." :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/48b2ab67ce7da1701a79f9ac0149a0aa.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}$. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/63dc4b8b2ede638834e47bd348f4e5d9.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $2$ units up to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}+2$. The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,1)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from from $y=0$ to $y=2$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/f8d53f5d2ab7fb698d8aaf146126ddfd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f4440-ba1a-58ce-9ff2-ccdf591a0d30" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Decay Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5837613-5ede-5efb-b535-33a630dad1fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113175} {:answer/id #uuid "a959d77c-aefe-5b06-b60c-162f70af36dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113176} {:answer/id #uuid "1937c2e6-6b3c-5add-9e7b-5e8f41a79a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113177} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1643c6-bbad-5bd3-8df1-2cc2d075a4bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113178} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8491c9-3385-56cb-bdef-3a0d4d3a34d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1937c2e6-6b3c-5add-9e7b-5e8f41a79a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1682/Source/Images/q-29377-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113177} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a68e3b6-23cf-51a3-a3cd-